.TH TOS_EXTRACT_SPRITES 1
.SH NAME
tos_extract_sprites \- convert DolDoc binary images to Inferno image files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 scripts/tos_extract_sprites.py
.I file
[
.B -o
.I outdir
]
[
.B --bin
.I n
]
[
.B --prefix
.I name
]
[
.B --compressed
]
[
.B --rgba
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tos_extract_sprites
is a host Python program (not a Dis module).
It reads DolDoc files that contain binary image or vector records, or
.B .GR
bitmaps, and writes Inferno
.IR image (6)
files:
an
.B m8
.B .bit
and a
.B k1
.B .mask
by default.
.PP
.B --compressed
selects Inferno's compressed image encoding.
.B --rgba
writes an
.B r8g8b8a8
image and an
.B a8
mask instead.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
	python3 scripts/tos_extract_sprites.py demo.HC -o /tmp/out --prefix demo
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /scripts/tos_extract_sprites.py
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR image (6),
.IR draw-image (2)
